<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Required once the app is signed with a Developer ID, because signing
         turns on the hardened runtime. Without this entitlement a
         non-sandboxed process is denied the microphone by TCC — silently —
         and Aircast captures nothing at all.

         NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist is only the prompt string;
         this is what actually lets the process reach Core Audio. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- Deliberately NOT set:
           com.apple.security.app-sandbox           (not shipping via the App Store)
           com.apple.security.get-task-allow        (notarization rejects it)
           com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
           com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
           com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit
         The ffmpeg sidecar is a static binary: it loads no external dylibs and
         JITs nothing, so it needs no exception. Tauri applies this same file to
         the sidecar as well as to Aircast itself, and every extra
         com.apple.security.cs.* weakens the runtime for both. -->
</dict>
</plist>
